=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
No network fault exists. The helpdesk ticket's premise is incorrect. A
thorough inspection of switch4, sshswitch, and router17 shows that both
VLAN 5 (10.5.0.0/24) and VLAN 6 (10.6.0.0/24) are fully operational from
end to end.

On switch4 the uplink (eth0) carries two tagged sub-interfaces: eth0.5 is
bridged into br_vlan5 alongside the VLAN-5 access ports (eth1, eth2, eth3,
eth6), and eth0.6 is bridged into br_vlan6 alongside the VLAN-6 access
ports (eth4, eth5). Neither VLAN is missing from the trunk — both have been
consistently configured.

On the upstream sshswitch (the multilayer switch that terminates the trunk),
br_v5 holds the VLAN 5 SVI at 10.5.0.254/24 and br_v6 holds the VLAN 6
SVI at 10.6.0.254/24. The respective bond sub-interfaces (bond0.5/bond0.6)
connect onward to router17 via the aggregated uplink, and the OSPF routing
table on sshswitch has correct entries for all campus subnets via 55.5.1.1
(router17).

Direct ping tests confirm every VLAN 5 host (pc1, pc2, dc_pc5) and every
VLAN 6 host (pc3, pc4) reaches its default gateway with zero packet loss,
and cross-VLAN pings to VLAN 10, 20, and 30 hosts also succeed.

Root cause: there is no fault. The maintenance team's visit did not alter
switch4's VLAN trunk configuration.

Corrective action: No configuration change is needed. The operations team
should verify the user-side experience (perhaps a DHCP lease renewal is
needed on affected endpoints) and close the ticket as a false alarm.
=== END ===
```